  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/init-co-jp/diff-tour/zipball/v0.5.0",
  "body": "The screens and the tours now come in Simplified Chinese, Traditional Chinese and Spanish, as well as English and Japanese.\n\n**What changed**\n\n- **Simplified Chinese (`zh`).** Builds on the work in #1 by @shangjinyu012-gif. Thank you!\n- **Traditional Chinese (`zh-Hant`).** Worded for readers in Taiwan (程式碼, 檔案, 資料表). Locales for Taiwan, Hong Kong and Macau pick it, and other Chinese locales pick Simplified Chinese.\n- **Spanish (`es`).** Neutral Spanish, picked by any `es_*` locale.\n- **Choosing a language.** The language is detected from your locale the first time you run `tour`. `tour setup` changes it, and `tour --lang zh`, `--lang zh-Hant` or `--lang es` changes it for one run. The tours and the answers to your questions are written in the same language.\n- **Example tours.** The example tour is now in [Simplified Chinese](https://github.com/init-co-jp/diff-tour/blob/main/tours/example-coupons.zh.json), [Traditional Chinese](https://github.com/init-co-jp/diff-tour/blob/main/tours/example-coupons.zh-Hant.json) and [Spanish](https://github.com/init-co-jp/diff-tour/blob/main/tours/example-coupons.es.json) too.\n- **Requests as issues.** We now take requests as issues and write the changes ourselves, instead of accepting pull requests. [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/init-co-jp/diff-tour/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) explains why. If something in your language sounds unnatural, please [open an issue](https://github.com/init-co-jp/diff-tour/issues/new/choose).\n\nPrompts for English and Japanese did not change, so tours you saved with v0.4.0 open as they are.\n\n**Install or update**\n\n```sh\ncurl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/init-co-jp/diff-tour/main/install.sh | sh\n```\n",
  "mentions_count": 1
}
